################################################################################
INVALID AS AUTHORITATIVE -- 2 of 4 legs ran the WRONG LIBRARY.  Marked 2026-10-09.
CLAUDE.md section 4: marked in place, never deleted.

WHAT IS WRONG
  The REF leg reported values BYTE-IDENTICAL to the M1 pre-fix leg
  (T_peak 1799.999258440192762, min Y -8.453045954736468e-12, front -51.267 cells),
  where A2_07 measured the post-fix library as 1799.998974446609736,
  -1.889798074490678e-11 and +3.499219221840 mm.
  The per-leg library hashes prove it: M1 and REF are BOTH 1eb0e2cb... (pre-fix).
  The post-fix library is 852555cf... and was never built in this run.

CAUSE, diagnosed not assumed
  The harness restored the post-fix source with `cp -p`, which PRESERVES THE BACKUP'S
  MTIME. That mtime is older than the object file already built from the M1-patched
  source, so ninja saw no work to do and the library was never rebuilt. M3 rebuilt
  correctly only because a python write advanced the mtime.

WHICH LEGS SURVIVE
  M1  VALID    pre-fix, deadBand 3, library 1eb0e2cb -> C5c FAIL. C5c is non-vacuous.
  REF INVALID  ran the pre-fix library. No post-fix reference was measured.
  M2  INVALID  reused REF's stale binary, so it is pre-fix + deadBand 1, not post-fix.
  M3  VALID    post-fix + heat x 0.9999, library 730e6c0d -> C5a FAIL by 84x. C5a is
               non-vacuous. (GATE_A3.md predicted ~83x before the run.)

THE INSTRUMENT DEFECT THIS EXPOSES
  run_c5_precision.sh asserted that the library hash CHANGED between its two legs.
  This harness printed the hash and asserted NOTHING about it, so it failed open --
  exactly the class CLAUDE.md section 8 exists to prevent ("authoritative only if the
  binary was demonstrably rebuilt against the exact source being tested"). What caught
  it was the reproduction control against A2_07, not the harness.

NOT SUPERSEDED BY THIS BANNER
  C5b NEVER FAILED on any leg, valid or not, and the invalid M2 points the OPPOSITE way
  from the mechanism GATE_A3.md section 3.2 registered: deadBand 1 gave |min Y| 6.20e-12,
  SMALLER than deadBand 3's 8.45e-12. That is a pre-registered stop condition and it is
  carried forward to the corrected run, not discarded with this log.
